Design of Experiments: One-at-a-Time (OAT) Sensitivity Analysis
================================================================================

Experiment Name: Liquidity Risk Model Sensitivity Analysis
Design Type: One-at-a-Time Perturbation Analysis
Purpose: Assess individual parameter impact on model outputs and identify critical factors

Analysis Framework:
------------------
Method: OAT with percentage perturbations around baseline
Baseline: Median operating conditions from historical data
Perturbation Levels: -50%, -25%, -10%, +10%, +25%, +50%
Replications: 50 per parameter setting
Total Runs: 1,950 (13 parameters × 6 levels × 25 base runs)

Base Case Parameters:
--------------------
RESERVE_RATIO: 0.125
PAYMENT_ARRIVAL_RATE: 125 payments/hour
AVERAGE_PAYMENT_SIZE: 250000 currency units
PAYMENT_SIZE_STDDEV: 100000 currency units
INTERBANK_CREDIT_LIMIT: 3000000 currency units
COLLATERAL_HAIRCUT: 0.20
LIQUIDITY_BUFFER: 5000000 currency units
QUEUE_PRIORITY_THRESHOLD: 300000 currency units
GRIDLOCK_RESOLUTION_TIME: 30 minutes
MARKET_VOLATILITY: 0.15
STRESS_EVENT_PROBABILITY: 0.02
SETTLEMENT_DELAY_MEAN: 2 minutes
CENTRAL_BANK_FACILITY_RATE: 0.05

Sensitivity Parameters:
======================

Parameter 1: RESERVE_RATIO
--------------------------
Description: Fraction of total assets held as liquid reserves
Baseline: 0.125 (12.5%)
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 0.0625
  -25%: 0.0938
  -10%: 0.1125
  +10%: 0.1375
  +25%: 0.1563
  +50%: 0.1875
Expected Impact: High on LCR, moderate on settlement times
Criticality: HIGH (regulatory requirement)

Parameter 2: PAYMENT_ARRIVAL_RATE
---------------------------------
Description: Average number of payments arriving per hour
Baseline: 125 payments/hour
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 62.5
  -25%: 93.75
  -10%: 112.5
  +10%: 137.5
  +25%: 156.25
  +50%: 187.5
Expected Impact: High on queue length and system capacity
Criticality: HIGH (operational capacity)

Parameter 3: AVERAGE_PAYMENT_SIZE
---------------------------------
Description: Mean value of individual payments
Baseline: 250000 currency units
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 125000
  -25%: 187500
  -10%: 225000
  +10%: 275000
  +25%: 312500
  +50%: 375000
Expected Impact: High on liquidity demands
Criticality: MEDIUM

Parameter 4: PAYMENT_SIZE_STDDEV
--------------------------------
Description: Standard deviation of payment amounts
Baseline: 100000 currency units
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 50000
  -25%: 75000
  -10%: 90000
  +10%: 110000
  +25%: 125000
  +50%: 150000
Expected Impact: Moderate on system volatility
Criticality: MEDIUM

Parameter 5: INTERBANK_CREDIT_LIMIT
-----------------------------------
Description: Maximum credit line between institutions
Baseline: 3000000 currency units
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 1500000
  -25%: 2250000
  -10%: 2700000
  +10%: 3300000
  +25%: 3750000
  +50%: 4500000
Expected Impact: High on gridlock prevention
Criticality: HIGH (systemic stability)

Parameter 6: COLLATERAL_HAIRCUT
-------------------------------
Description: Discount applied to collateral value
Baseline: 0.20 (20%)
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 0.10
  -25%: 0.15
  -10%: 0.18
  +10%: 0.22
  +25%: 0.25
  +50%: 0.30
Expected Impact: Moderate on available liquidity
Criticality: MEDIUM

Parameter 7: LIQUIDITY_BUFFER
-----------------------------
Description: Additional cash reserves for emergencies
Baseline: 5000000 currency units
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 2500000
  -25%: 3750000
  -10%: 4500000
  +10%: 5500000
  +25%: 6250000
  +50%: 7500000
Expected Impact: Moderate on stress resilience
Criticality: MEDIUM

Parameter 8: QUEUE_PRIORITY_THRESHOLD
-------------------------------------
Description: Payment size threshold for priority processing
Baseline: 300000 currency units
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 150000
  -25%: 225000
  -10%: 270000
  +10%: 330000
  +25%: 375000
  +50%: 450000
Expected Impact: Moderate on settlement efficiency
Criticality: LOW

Parameter 9: GRIDLOCK_RESOLUTION_TIME
-------------------------------------
Description: Maximum time allowed before gridlock intervention
Baseline: 30 minutes
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 15 minutes
  -25%: 22.5 minutes
  -10%: 27 minutes
  +10%: 33 minutes
  +25%: 37.5 minutes
  +50%: 45 minutes
Expected Impact: High on operational risk
Criticality: HIGH

Parameter 10: MARKET_VOLATILITY
-------------------------------
Description: Standard deviation of asset price changes
Baseline: 0.15 (15%)
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 0.075
  -25%: 0.1125
  -10%: 0.135
  +10%: 0.165
  +25%: 0.1875
  +50%: 0.225
Expected Impact: High on collateral value fluctuations
Criticality: HIGH (market risk)

Parameter 11: STRESS_EVENT_PROBABILITY
--------------------------------------
Description: Daily probability of extreme market event
Baseline: 0.02 (2% per day)
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 0.01
  -25%: 0.015
  -10%: 0.018
  +10%: 0.022
  +25%: 0.025
  +50%: 0.03
Expected Impact: Moderate on tail risk
Criticality: MEDIUM

Parameter 12: SETTLEMENT_DELAY_MEAN
-----------------------------------
Description: Average processing time for payment settlement
Baseline: 2 minutes
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 1 minute
  -25%: 1.5 minutes
  -10%: 1.8 minutes
  +10%: 2.2 minutes
  +25%: 2.5 minutes
  +50%: 3 minutes
Expected Impact: Moderate on throughput
Criticality: MEDIUM

Parameter 13: CENTRAL_BANK_FACILITY_RATE
----------------------------------------
Description: Interest rate for central bank emergency lending
Baseline: 0.05 (5% annual)
Perturbation Levels:
  -50%: 0.025
  -25%: 0.0375
  -10%: 0.045
  +10%: 0.055
  +25%: 0.0625
  +50%: 0.075
Expected Impact: Low on facility usage decisions
Criticality: LOW

Response Metrics:
----------------
Primary Responses:
1. Liquidity Coverage Ratio (LCR)
2. Net Stable Funding Ratio (NSFR)
3. Maximum Queue Length
4. Average Settlement Time
5. Gridlock Events per Day
6. System Throughput (payments/hour)

Secondary Responses:
7. 95th Percentile Settlement Time
8. Collateral Utilization Rate
9. Interbank Credit Usage
10. Central Bank Facility Draws
11. Payment Rejection Rate
12. Intraday Liquidity Shortfall

Experimental Procedure:
======================

Phase 1: Baseline Validation (Runs 1-50)
----------------------------------------
- Run baseline scenario 50 times
- Establish reference distributions for all responses
- Calculate baseline mean, std dev, 95% CI for each metric
- Verify model stability and randomness

Phase 2: Parameter Perturbations (Runs 51-1950)
-----------------------------------------------
For each parameter i = 1 to 13:
  For each perturbation level j = 1 to 6:
    Run 25 replications
    Record all response metrics
    Calculate sensitivity index: SI = (ΔY/Y₀)/(Δx/x₀)

Phase 3: Analysis
-----------------
1. Calculate absolute sensitivity: |ΔResponse|/|ΔParameter|
2. Calculate relative sensitivity: (ΔResponse/Response₀)/(ΔParameter/Parameter₀)
3. Generate tornado diagrams for each response
4. Rank parameters by impact magnitude
5. Identify critical parameters (high sensitivity)
6. Assess parameter interaction indicators
7. Define acceptable parameter ranges

Sensitivity Index Calculation:
------------------------------
For parameter x and response y:

Absolute Sensitivity:
  S_abs = Δy/Δx = (y_perturbed - y_baseline)/(x_perturbed - x_baseline)

Relative Sensitivity:
  S_rel = (Δy/y_baseline)/(Δx/x_baseline)

Normalized Sensitivity:
  S_norm = (y_perturbed - y_baseline)/σ_baseline

Where σ_baseline is the standard deviation at baseline

